  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Installation of wooden tree house structure in rear garden (Retrospective); addition of fixed privacy screening to two elevations&nbsp; Structure is for incidental domestic use only",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;div&gt;The existing treehouse, notwithstanding the addition of the screening and relocation of the stairs, by reason of its location, orientation and siting in close proximity to the boundaries of no. 55 and 59 Canons Drive, results in a harmful loss of privacy with regard to actual and perceived overlooking of the neighbouring residents, to the detriment of the visual and residential amenities of these neighbouring occupiers, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3.D(7) of The London Plan (2021), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies (2013) and the Adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
